<section class="section">
	<h2>Two modes</h2>
	<p>Switch with <code>/librarian</code> and <code>/researcher</code>. Each mode has its own tools and its own model.</p>
	<div class="cards">
		<div class="card">
			<p class="tag">Librarian</p>
			<h3>Keeps the library in order</h3>
			<ul>
				<li>Tags from your own tag list, proposed in review notes that you edit</li>
				<li>Imports by DOI, PMID or ISBN, with abstracts and citekeys</li>
				<li>Metadata repair, duplicates, retractions, open-access PDFs</li>
				<li>No web access: outside data comes only through its import and repair tools</li>
			</ul>
		</div>
		<div class="card">
			<p class="tag">Researcher</p>
			<h3>Reads and searches</h3>
			<ul>
				<li>"What do I have on …?" answered from your library</li>
				<li>PubMed and OpenAlex searches that show what you already have</li>
				<li>Literature notes and syntheses in your notes folder, with a source for every claim</li>
				<li>Cannot change the library, except to add a short linked note</li>
			</ul>
		</div>
	</div>
</section>

<section class="section split">
	<div>
		<h2>You approve every change</h2>
		<p>Before any change to your library, Sub-Sub asks the Zotero server for a preview and shows it to you. The change runs only after you select Yes. This check is in the program, not in the instructions to the model, so the model cannot skip it.</p>
		<p>Every change is recorded in a journal. <code>/history</code> lists recent changes and <code>/undo</code> reverts one. Nothing is deleted: items go to the Zotero trash, tags are removed from items.</p>
		<p><a href="/privacy/">Privacy and safety</a></p>
	</div>
	<div>
		<h2>A profile for how you work</h2>
		<div class="table-wrap">
		<table>
			<thead><tr><th>Profile</th><th>What Sub-Sub does</th></tr></thead>
			<tbody>
				<tr><td>Reader</td><td>Explains each step. Reading notes are quotes with page numbers and questions for you. No summaries.</td></tr>
				<tr><td>Scholar</td><td>Literature notes, syntheses, searches and alerts. The full librarian.</td></tr>
				<tr><td>Author</td><td>Scholar, plus manuscripts: citation check, bibliography, comments on the argument.</td></tr>
				<tr><td>Editor</td><td>Everything, including drafted manuscript text when you ask.</td></tr>
			</tbody>
		</table>
		</div>
		<p><a href="/profiles/">About profiles</a></p>
	</div>
</section>

